# .spool/scanner/scanner.req

feature: SCANNER

requirements:
  - id: SCANNER-1
    title: Annotation Detection
    description: >
      The scanner must detect valid Spool ID annotations
      in test files and record their location.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Annotations are comment lines containing nothing but a valid
      Spool ID. Keeping the annotation format strict eliminates
      false positives and establishes an unambiguous convention.
      ID normalization is applied at scan time so the rest of the
      system operates on canonical IDs only.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: SCANNER-1-1
        title: Annotation Detected
        description: >
          Given a test file containing a comment line with a valid
          Spool ID optionally followed by a colon and title,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the annotation is detected and its line number recorded.

      - id: SCANNER-1-2
        title: Non-Canonical Normalized
        description: >
          Given a test file containing a comment line with a valid
          Spool ID in non-canonical form (lowercase, leading zeros),
          when the file is scanned,
          then the annotation is detected and its ID normalized
          to canonical form.

      - id: SCANNER-1-3
        title: Extra Content Ignored
        description: >
          Given a test file containing a comment line with additional
          content alongside a valid Spool ID,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the line is not treated as an annotation.

      - id: SCANNER-1-4
        title: No Annotations Empty Result
        description: >
          Given a test file containing no annotations,
          when the file is scanned,
          then an empty result is returned and no error is produced.

  - id: SCANNER-2
    title: Annotation Association
    description: >
      The scanner must associate detected annotations with the
      test function that follows them, regardless of what
      appears between the annotation and the function.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Association is based on the next test function following
      an annotation rather than the next non-blank line, because
      line numbers are fragile and function names are the meaningful
      unit of traceability. Intervening blank lines, comments, or
      other non-test content should not break the association.
      Interpreter plugins are responsible for identifying test
      function boundaries.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: SCANNER-2-1
        title: Immediate Association
        description: >
          Given an annotation immediately followed by a test function,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the annotation is associated with that test function.

      - id: SCANNER-2-2
        title: Separated Association
        description: >
          Given an annotation separated from the next test function
          by blank lines or non-test code,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the annotation is still associated with that
          test function.

      - id: SCANNER-2-3
        title: Stacked Annotations
        description: >
          Given multiple stacked annotations immediately preceding
          a test function,
          when the file is scanned,
          then all stacked annotations are associated with
          that test function.

      - id: SCANNER-2-4
        title: Same ID Multiple Functions
        description: >
          Given a single AC ID annotating multiple test functions,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the ID is associated with all annotated test functions.

      - id: SCANNER-2-5
        title: Orphaned Annotation
        description: >
          Given an annotation with no following test function
          in the file,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the annotation is recorded as orphaned and
          no error is produced.

  - id: SCANNER-3
    title: Interpreter Registry
    description: >
      The scanner must maintain a registry of compiled-in
      interpreters and select the appropriate one for each
      test file.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Pluggable interpreters keep the scanner language agnostic
      while allowing language-specific test function extraction.
      Interpreter selection is driven by the configured test_patterns
      so that pattern configuration and interpreter availability
      are naturally coupled. Files with no matching interpreter
      are skipped gracefully.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: SCANNER-3-1
        title: Matching Interpreter Selected
        description: >
          Given a test file whose name matches a configured
          test_pattern and a registered interpreter that supports
          that filename,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the matching interpreter is used for test
          function extraction.

      - id: SCANNER-3-2
        title: No Interpreter Warning
        description: >
          Given a test file whose name matches a configured
          test_pattern but no registered interpreter supports
          that filename,
          when the file is scanned,
          then the file is skipped and a warning is recorded.

      - id: SCANNER-3-3
        title: First Match Wins
        description: >
          Given multiple registered interpreters,
          when a test file is scanned,
          then the first interpreter whose Supports() returns
          true for that filename is used.

  - id: SCANNER-4
    title: Compiled-in Interpreters
    description: >
      Spool must ship with compiled-in interpreters covering
      mainstream testing frameworks.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Providing interpreters for Go, JUnit, Jest, and Playwright
      out of the box means Spool is immediately useful for the
      majority of real-world codebases without requiring any
      additional setup or community contributions.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: SCANNER-4-1
        title: Go Test Extraction
        description: >
          Given a Go test file,
          when test functions are extracted,
          then all functions matching the Test* naming convention
          with a *testing.T parameter are returned with their
          names and line numbers.

      - id: SCANNER-4-2
        title: JUnit Test Extraction
        description: >
          Given a JUnit test file,
          when test functions are extracted,
          then all methods annotated with @Test are returned
          with their names and line numbers.

      - id: SCANNER-4-3
        title: Jest Test Extraction
        description: >
          Given a Jest test file,
          when test functions are extracted,
          then all it() and test() calls are returned with
          their description strings and line numbers.

      - id: SCANNER-4-4
        title: Playwright Test Extraction
        description: >
          Given a Playwright test file,
          when test functions are extracted,
          then all test() calls from @playwright/test are
          returned with their description strings and
          line numbers.

  - id: SCANNER-5
    title: Interpreter Interface
    description: >
      Spool must publish a stable interpreter interface
      that allows third parties to implement and register
      custom interpreters.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Publishing the interpreter interface lowers the barrier
      for community contributions and allows teams with
      non-mainstream testing frameworks to extend Spool
      without forking the project. The interface is intentionally
      minimal to keep the implementation burden low.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: SCANNER-5-1
        title: Third-Party Registration
        description: >
          Given a third-party interpreter that implements the
          Interpreter interface,
          when it is registered with the scanner,
          then it participates in interpreter selection alongside
          compiled-in interpreters.

      - id: SCANNER-5-2
        title: Minimal Interface Contract
        description: >
          Given the published Interpreter interface,
          then it must expose only Supports(filename string) bool
          and ExtractTestFunctions(filename string, contents []byte)
          as required methods.

  - id: SCANNER-6
    title: Scanner Error Handling
    description: >
      The scanner must handle unreadable or unparseable test
      files gracefully without crashing the language server.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Consistent with the parser's fault tolerance philosophy,
      a single bad test file must never destabilize the index
      or crash the LSP. Errors are recorded as diagnostics
      and scanning continues.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: SCANNER-6-1
        title: Unreadable File Continuity
        description: >
          Given a test file that cannot be read,
          when the file is scanned,
          then an error is recorded for that file and
          scanning continues for all remaining files.

      - id: SCANNER-6-2
        title: Unparseable File Continuity
        description: >
          Given a test file that cannot be parsed by its interpreter,
          when the file is scanned,
          then an error is recorded for that file and
          scanning continues for all remaining files.